// spec ch05 §5.12 / book ch11-01: a by-value capture becomes an
// *owned* field of the closure object, so capturing a reference-typed
// local by value copies the referent -- never the reference. The copy
// is therefore independent of the original: mutating `x` after the
// closure is built must not be visible through the capture.
int main() {
    int x = 7;
    int& r = x;
    auto i = [r]() { return r; };
    x = 99;
    return i() - 7;
}
